stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> drafted : CI1, an active retiral enrollment and a period close

    drafted --> held : CI2, no PRAN for an NPS enrollment, BEN-22
    held --> drafted : CI3, PRAN supplied or issued
    drafted --> void : CI4, the enrollment was suspended for the whole period, no amount arises

    drafted --> validated : CI5, employer and employee amounts resolved against the wage basis and the regime rate
    validated --> batched : CI6, a period batch assembles the validated instructions for one scheme
    batched --> handed_over : CI7, the manifest is handed to the employer for upload while the file layout stays fenced on B11
    handed_over --> acknowledged : CI8, the CRA or trustee reference is recorded, only now is the period remitted
    handed_over --> rejected : CI9, the CRA or trustee rejects the line, the reason is stored as received

    rejected --> superseded : CI10, a correcting instruction names the one it replaces
    validated --> superseded : CI11, a retro wage or rate correction re-values the period
    acknowledged --> superseded : CI11

    superseded --> [*]
    acknowledged --> [*]
    void --> [*]

    note right of handed_over
        No CRA file layout is specified in this PRD.
        The product emits an internal manifest and records
        the employer's own upload, B11. Nothing is marked
        remitted without an acknowledgement reference, BEN-21.
    end note

    note left of validated
        Tier II is tagged and never produces an instruction.
        VPF rides the ECR and never produces one either.
        Only the employer share reaches the retiral cap ledger.
    end note
